---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { breadcrumbs } from '../lib/schema';
import { GOOGLE } from '../config/site';

/**
 * Written from what the app and the order server do today (the app's
 * docs/play-store/data-safety.md). The privacy lawyer reviews it before the
 * apps go to production: the face-recognition paragraph, the retention of paid
 * orders and the rights sections are the points to check. Change it in the
 * same commit as anything the app starts or stops sending.
 */
const UPDATED = 'October 9, 2026';
const EMAIL = 'info@photo-to-text.com';

const trail = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Privacy policy', path: '/privacy-policy/' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | BabyBookAI"
  description="What BabyBookAI does with your photos and your order details: your library is read on your phone, and only the finished book is sent to be printed."
  schema={[breadcrumbs(trail)]}
  cta="privacy-policy"
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={trail} />

  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pb-20 pt-8">
    <p class="font-extrabold uppercase tracking-wider text-teal">Privacy</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-[2.6rem] text-teal sm:text-6xl">Your baby’s photos stay on your phone</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-ink-soft">Privacy policy · Last updated: {UPDATED}</p>

    <div class="mt-10 rounded-card border-2 border-hair bg-surface p-6 sm:p-10">

    <p class="text-lg">
      BabyBookAI (“we”) is an app that makes a printed photo book of your baby’s first year from the
      photos on your phone. It is a Photo-to-Text product. Contact{' '}
      <a class="text-teal underline" href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl text-teal">The short version</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
      <li>Your photo library is read <strong>on your phone</strong>. We never see it.</li>
      <li>
        When you order a book, the finished book file (the photos you chose, your words, your baby’s
        name) is sent to us and to our printer.
      </li>
      <li>
        To deliver it we need your name, email and address. Payment is handled by Stripe; we never
        see your card.
      </li>
      <li>The app has no advertising, no analytics, no tracking and no account.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl text-teal">What the app does on your phone</h2>
    <p class="mt-4">
      To choose the photos, the app reads the photos in your library from the months you pick: their
      dates, sizes, sharpness and duplicates. This happens only on your phone, and nothing about your
      library is sent anywhere.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4">
      <strong>Recognizing your baby (optional).</strong> If you turn on the recognition switch before
      the scan, the app learns your baby’s face from photos you tap, on your phone, to keep other
      people’s children out of the book. The face data exists only in the phone’s memory during the
      scan and is deleted when the scan ends; it is never saved or sent. The switch is off by default
      and is not offered in Illinois, Texas or Washington.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4">
      The book you are working on is saved on your phone so you can come back to it. It holds which
      photos are in it, your words, and where faces are in those photos (to frame them), never face
      data. Starting a new book deletes it, as does uninstalling the app.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl text-teal">What we receive, and why</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full border-collapse text-left text-base">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-hair text-ink-soft">
            <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold">What</th>
            <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-semibold">Why</th>
            <th class="py-2 font-semibold">Shared with</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="align-top">
          <tr class="border-b border-hair">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">
              The book file: the photos in your book, your words, your baby’s name and birth year
            </td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">To print your book</td>
            <td class="py-3">Gelato (our printer)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-hair">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">Number of pages, currency</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">To price the order</td>
            <td class="py-3">—</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-hair">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">Your name, email, shipping address, phone (optional)</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">To deliver the book and send the receipt</td>
            <td class="py-3">Gelato (delivery), Stripe (receipt)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">Payment details</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">To take payment</td>
            <td class="py-3">Stripe only; we never receive them</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4">
      We use this information only to make, ship and support your order. We do not sell it, use it for
      advertising, or use your photos for anything other than printing your book.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl text-teal">Who else handles it</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
      <li>
        <strong>Stripe</strong> processes payments
        (<a class="text-teal underline" href="https://stripe.com/privacy">stripe.com/privacy</a>).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Gelato</strong> prints and ships the book
        (<a class="text-teal underline" href="https://www.gelato.com/legal/privacy"
          >gelato.com/legal/privacy</a
        >).
      </li>
      <li>Our order server, where the book file waits until it reaches the printer.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl text-teal">How long we keep it</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
      <li>Orders that are never paid are deleted, with their book file, after 7 days.</li>
      <li>
        For paid orders we keep the order details and the book file for as long as we need to deliver
        the order, support you, and meet tax and accounting rules. You can ask us to delete them at
        any time (see below).
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl text-teal">Your rights, and how to delete your data</h2>
    <p class="mt-4">
      You can ask us for a copy of your data, to correct it, or to delete it, by writing to
      <a class="text-teal underline" href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a> from the email address you
      ordered with, naming BabyBookAI. We will answer within 30 days. To delete your data, tell us
      “delete my data”: we then delete your order details and your book file, except what the law
      obliges us to keep, and ask Gelato and Stripe to delete theirs.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4">
      If you live in the European Union or the United Kingdom, you can also complain to your data
      protection authority. We handle your order details because you asked us to make and ship your
      book, and, if you use it, face recognition only with your consent, which you can withdraw by
      turning the switch off.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl text-teal">This website</h2>
    {
      GOOGLE.analyticsId ? (
        <p class="mt-4">
          babybookai.com uses Google Analytics to count visits and see which pages are read, through
          cookies set by Google. It receives your IP address, browser and the pages you visit, never
          anything from the app. You can block it with your browser’s settings or Google’s opt-out
          add-on (<a class="text-teal underline" href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout</a>).
          Google’s policy: <a class="text-teal underline" href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
        </p>
      ) : (
        <p class="mt-4">babybookai.com sets no cookies and runs no analytics or advertising scripts.</p>
      )
    }

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl text-teal">Children</h2>
    <p class="mt-4">
      BabyBookAI is for parents. It is not directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect
      information from children. The photos of your baby are used only to print your book.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl text-teal">Security</h2>
    <p class="mt-4">
      Everything sent from the app travels encrypted (HTTPS). Book files are stored in a private
      folder on our server and reach the printer only through a signed, expiring link.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl text-teal">Changes</h2>
    <p class="mt-4">We will post any changes here and update the date above.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
